<Article
  title="One shell, several lives"
  description="Aura is one finished room on a steel skid. A stay, a glass deck, a small resort, a farm wall, or water from the air are different uses of that same shell."
  kicker="The story"
  date="2026-09-30"
>
  <p>Aura starts as a finished room you can add to land you already have. It sits on a steel skid. The glass is smooth: clear, mirror, or tint. That room is the product. Everything else on this site is a way of using it.</p>
  <h2>What the shell can be</h2>
  <p>As a room, it is an extension or a small stay. As glass, it lifts onto helical piles, with a floor lit from beneath and a deck. As a resort, a few of those rooms are planned for a site in Canada or Costa Rica, built custom. Costa Rica does not have its photograph yet. The snow is the reference until it does.</p>
  <p>As a farm, one long side becomes a vertical aeroponic wall. As H20, an atmospheric generator would sit on the roof and a short bottling line would sit inside. That water unit comes later, and it still needs further research. The shell does not stop being a room. The work changes.</p>
  <h2>What you can do now</h2>
  <p>You can ask Aura to build a room, or a farm unit, and place it. You can buy one and use it yourself: live in it, let it, or grow in it. Bottling waits on H20. The <a href="/builder">builder</a> is the tool for walking the clearing and setting a shell. It does not sell, and it does not open an account. The source is on <a href="https://github.com/kr8tiv-ai/aura-homes">GitHub</a>.</p>
  <h2>What we hope</h2>
  <p>The longer hope is a network in which food and water from these shells are free to the person who takes them, because an advertiser has paid to put their name on the harvest or the jug. That network is described in <a href="/journal/free-food-and-water">its own note</a>. It is not operating today. Saying so plainly is part of the offer.</p>
  <p>If you want the room first, start at <a href="/#shell">the shell</a>. If you want the farm or the water, those pages say what is added, and what is still a hope.</p>
</Article>
